  "notes": "**Goal:** Lean muscle, V-taper/hourglass emphasis\n**Priority muscles:** Lateral delts, rear delts, lats/upper back, glute max, glute medius\n**Moderate:** Chest, arms, quads, hamstrings, calves, abs\n\n## Weekly Volume\n\n| Muscle | Sets/week | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lateral delts | 10 | High |\n| Rear delts | 6 (+ indirect from ~9 row sets) | High |\n| Lats / upper back | 14 | High |\n| Glute max | 6 direct (+ squat/RDL/BSS overlap) | High |\n| Glute medius | 6 (+ BSS) | High |\n| Chest | 10 | Moderate |\n| Quads | ~11 | Moderate |\n| Hamstrings | 10 | Moderate |\n| Calves | 3 standing + 3 seated | Moderate |\n| Biceps / triceps | 4 each (+ indirect) | Moderate |\n\n## Execution Rules\n\n- **Proximity to failure:** Most sets end 0–3 reps short of failure. Isolation work (lateral raises, curls, leg extensions) can go closer; heavy squats and RDLs stay further away.\n- **Progression:** Add reps within the listed range first. Once you hit the top of the range on all sets, add weight and drop back to the bottom.\n- **Lateral raise technique:** Lead with the elbows, stop around shoulder height, control the lowering phase. Light enough that there's no torso swing.\n- **Rest:** 2–3 min on compounds, 60–90 sec on isolation.\n\n## Nutrition\n\nLean bulk is the right call here — muscle mass is the limiting factor for a \"ripped\" look, not body fat.\n\n- **Calories:** ~250–350 above maintenance per day\n- **Rate of gain:** 0.25–0.5% of body weight per month (~0.4–0.8 lb)\n- **Protein:** 115–160 g/day (1.6–2.2 g/kg)\n\nIf you're newer to lifting, eating at maintenance can build muscle while losing fat, just more slowly.\n\n## Changes From the Original Draft\n\n1. Lateral delts raised from 7 → 10 sets/week\n2. Rear delts raised from 4 → 6 sets/week\n3. Quads cut from ~15 → ~11 sets/week (dropped leg press and one leg-extension slot)\n4. Lower A calf raise switched from seated to standing\n5. Hip thrusts moved to the first slot on Lower A\n6. Upper B's redundant second lat pulldown replaced with single-arm cable pulldown\n7. Optional: swap Upper B dips/machine press for seated DB overhead press (don't add on top)\n\n## Supporting Research\n\n- Schoenfeld et al. (2017) — dose-response of weekly set volume to hypertrophy\n- Pelland et al. (2024) — volume meta-analysis; compound sets count ~0.5 for secondary muscles\n- Schoenfeld et al. (2016) — training frequency, 2x/week per muscle\n- Maeo et al. (2023) — overhead triceps extension vs. pressdown\n- Maeo et al. (2021) — seated vs. lying leg curl\n- Kinoshita et al. (2023) — standing vs. seated calf raise\n- Simão et al. (2012) — exercise order\n- Morton et al. (2018) — protein intake meta-analysis\n\n*General training guidance, not medical advice. See a professional for injury or medical concerns.*\n"
